I'm becoming less enamored of eggs (as a food, in NetHack)
all the time.  By the time you have a unicorn horn for dealing
with the routine deleterious effects that occur after practically
every egg you eat (well, maybe only two thirds of them), food
just isn't so scarce that you can't afford to skip the eggs.  Do
I really want to eat something that's going to confuse and
stun me several turns later at possibly a very inconvenient
time?  Nah, I think I'll just eat one of those extra C-rats.

Pre-Sokoban, it is occasionally necessary to eat eggs,
despite consequences, merely because food is scarce.
But pre-Sokoban, cockatrice eggs are fortunately rather
unlikely, in my experience thus far.  (Then again, if
other people are running into minotaurs on DL9, maybe
cockatrices sometimes start showing up on DL4, and
the RNG is just being nice to me?)

I do _carry_ eggs that I find, if I can afford space in main
inventory.  I got a pet yellow dragon that way once, which
was significantly beneficial to my game.  (Unfortunately
I got myself killed by a collapsing drawbridge later.)
After a while, when I've got about four eggs and none
of them have hatched and I need the inventory space,
I unload them into a stash chest.


